## Refactoring & Removal Discipline
- **Removal is deliverable**: "Remove" or "replace" means delete old code, not wrap.
- **Fix tests, don't preserve them**: Broken tests after removal = expected cost, not signal for compatibility.
- **No unwanted backward compatibility**: Compatibility layers only for external consumers or explicit request.
- **Tests pass ≠ issue complete**: Verify behavior matches the spec and downstream consumers actually use it, not only that tests pass.
- When building agent skills, extract mechanical operations into bundled scripts so the agent focuses on judgment, not procedure.

## Review Quality
- **Model diversity required**: All reviews (code, spec, plan) include at least one reviewer from different model than orchestrating session, plus any current-model reviewers.
{{- if ne $agent "pi" }}
- **External dispatch**: Claude CLI, Codex, Cursor, Gemini add perspectives beyond built-in peer pairing; include one when available via `dispatch-external-model` skill.
{{- end }}
{{- if eq $agent "claude" }}
- **Claude pairing**: Use Opus when orchestrating on Sonnet, Sonnet when orchestrating on Opus; do not use Haiku for review.
- **Dispatch in Claude Code**: Dispatch peer Claude via Agent tool with `model` override; use `dispatch-external-model` skill for external tools.
{{- else if eq $agent "pi" }}
- **Dispatch in Pi**: Pi has built-in multi-model support via `pi-subagents` — use it for review diversity rather than spawning external CLIs. Route review subagents to `claude-bridge/`{{ if $personal }} or `openai-codex/`{{ else if $work }} or `cursor/`{{ end }} providers.
{{- else }}
- **Dispatch**: Use native agent dispatch when available; consult `dispatch-external-model` skill for CLI-based dispatch.
{{- end }}
